{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T16:55:59.888Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dec610b5c29dc08047ecfcc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1726","claim:pm-gh1727","claim:pm-gh1728","claim:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1726+pm-gh1727+pm-gh1728+pm-gh1729","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1726","claim:pm-gh1727","claim:pm-gh1728","claim:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T16:55:59.888Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-14T16:55:59.879Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Root cause (2026-11-14): the direct-caller occurrence recorder flattens an array into one attached occurrence per entry, so [] produced zero occurrences and strict validation had nothing to check; for a non-list flag the coercer mapped each entry, so [true], [1,2] and ['a','b'] also reached handlers as arrays although argv keeps the last occurrence and never delivers one. Fix: refuseDirectDeclarationViolations refuses any array for a flag that is not list/repeatable (extension_flag_value_invalid with flag) and treats [] on a required list as missing. Two more defects in the same seam: (1) on the built CLI a bare repeatable boolean switch reached the handler as [] (pm demo --many -> []), because Commander calls the list accumulator with undefined for a value-less switch and list flattening drops undefined; fixed in applyDynamicExtensionFlagOptions (each bare occurrence records true). (2) PmClient.run applied the native-field array rewrites (tags joined to CSV; dep, comment, file, test and others promoted to arrays) to extension actions too, so a declared scalar --dep would have received ['x']; optionsWithAuthor now takes nativeAction and extension actions keep the caller's values. The mixed attached/bare ordering edge (--many=false --many keeps only [false]) is filed as pm-g2zzus."}]}],"before_hash":"687c63c57ce9ef110522b9615e935e804055b8ed99eaae051d3da39e9ec8940d","after_hash":"9eb6e293f5227bbfe9c5475e76994bc938c4b8666970cc06f5c37b23c96eb8b7","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0cdb09a9a356d5fc82967d9360e493c9d3fd5165ec5806443bc8c1a02d4fc758"}
